OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking)
1. PRE-EXISTING, not this change (markup byte-identical to master; git diff master touches none of it): axe "incomplete" aria-prohibited-attr on .badge-tier spans that carry aria-label with no role, and color-contrast needs-review on aria-hidden glyphs inside .status badges (flags heading, ledger status column).
2. .tier3-oracle sets list-style:none. Chromium keeps the list semantics (confirmed in the accessibility tree); Safari/VoiceOver historically drops list semantics for list-style:none lists. ACCESSIBILITY.md and WCAG 2.2 AA are silent, so this is not a failure; adding role="list" would harden it.
3. The pill fill vs the drawer surface is 1.12-1.33:1. Not a 1.4.11 issue because the meaning is carried by the visible text ("ok"/"missing") at >= 6.79:1, not by the pill boundary. Same pattern as every other badge on the page.
4. Stale-report branch (hasReport=true) is not exercised by the shipped fixtures (their report.md files were deleted); I verified it via a scratch fixture copy. The panel then shows a warning that the gate rejects the row beside four "ok" items, which is an accurate rendering of the oracle checks but could read as contradictory. Content/design call for the lead, not an accessibility criterion.
5. Evidence method: axe-cli covers the light scheme by default; dark scheme was audited with the same axe-core inside Playwright emulating prefers-color-scheme:dark (the dashboard's only theme switch). Page JS was not exercised beyond loading; the SSE client is unchanged by this task.
